<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexey Kaledin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1861">1861</a>–<a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexey Kaledin was a Russian cavalry general and the first elected ataman of the Don <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossacks</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/february-revolution">February Revolution</a> of 1917. A successful army commander in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, he refused to recognise the Bolshevik seizure of power and gave refuge to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volunteer-army">Volunteer Army</a> on the Don. As Cossacks deserted and Red forces advanced, he shot himself in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/novocherkassk">Novocherkassk</a> in February 1918.</p></div>
